<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I upgraded it from a previous version of OpenGD77. <br>I just followed your directions exactly, turn radio off.  Remove the battery and reinstalled it and held down the SK1 and SK2 while turning it back on.  I was then able to get it into  DFU mode, and successfully upgraded the firmware.<br>Thanks! <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"> It's working again!</div></blockquote>Probably you had some sort of glitch when the firmware file was being uploaded from your PC.<br><br>FYI.<br><br>The CPU in the radio has a way to latch the power to the radio, i.e a FET in parallel with the On/Off switch, so that turning off the switch does not guarantee that the radio is actually being turned off.<br><br>The reason the CPU needs this control is to allow the CPU to hold the power for a short while after you turn off the radio so that it can save the settings.<br><br>However, if something goes wrong with the upload, this override can remain on, and hence you have to take the battery out.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Jul 18, 2023 5:37 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
