		<title type="html"><![CDATA[New Beta version 2023 07 15]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3044&amp;p=24443#p24443"><![CDATA[
A new Beta version is now available with some new functionality and various bug fixes<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/GD77/42a91ba8c79faafda13733eb2ca8cd0a00d49cdc" class="postlink">downloads/GD77/42a91ba8c79faafda13733eb2ca8cd0a00d49cdc</a><br><br>or <br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/GD77/Latest" class="postlink">downloads/GD77/Latest</a><br><br>• Add “Night” theme system. This feature is primarily for colour radios e.g. UV380, a where separate Night theme can be uploaded.<br><br>On monochrome radios like the GD77 and MD9600, the Auto night theme is also available but because these radios do not have a colour display, this feature inverts the colour of the display. i.e During the night, the screen has a black background with white text.<br><br>Theme can automatically switch between day and night themes if Options -&gt; Display options - &gt; Auto night is enabled (On), and also the clock and location is set.<br>Automatic Day / Night switching uses the position of the sun to determine whether Day or Night theme should be used.<br><br>Day / Night theme can also be manually toggled <br>SK1 + Red toggles (overrides) Day/Night, and disables auto night/day<br>SK1 + longpress RED clears the override (and re-enable auto night/day) <br><br>Note. Automatic Day/Night theme switching is checked every 5 minutes.<br><br>• Added Night brightness. Options -&gt; Display options -&gt; Nite Bright.   The night brightness value is used in conjunction with the Day / Night theme system, as described above.<br><br>• If a Quick Key is assigned to increase or decrease the normal brightness value; when the radio is in Night theme mode, the same Quick Key will change the Night Bright value, so that the brightness can be adjusted regardless of  Day/Night theme mode.<br><br>• Fix "No Keys" beep option access when VP pack is not found in flash.<br><br>• Change  text “Bandwidth” in the Channel details to “BW” because the text of Bandwidth was too long and caused cropping of the bandwidth unit (kHz).<br>Note. All translated text which was too long, has also been changed to “BW”<br><br>• Do not attempt to save the settings or VFO when Flash memory test has failed<br><br>• Fix reverseRepeater / displayChannelSetting / monitorMode in VFO<br><br>• Internal changes  to the way the buttons/keys are detected for monitor mode.<br><br>• Add missing voice prompt, and update voice prompts to support the new functionality<br>See <a href="https://opengd77.com/downloads/Voice_Prompts/Latest" class="postlink">https://opengd77.com/downloads/Voice_Prompts/Latest</a><br><br>Thanks go to Daniel F1RMB, for creating all these fixes and enhancements<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Jul 15, 2023 7:47 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
